Message-ID: <7F35DC84-3935-4465-89BD-B06D1D9B3552@ebi.ac.uk>

Hi Teresa,
The Ensembl mart attributes are set up as 4 separate categories or  
"pages". If you take a look at the martview interface you will see  
that these categories are: Features, Homologs, Structures, Sequences  
and Variations. At present, it is not possible to mix attributes from  
multiple sections as you will get the error message you received (i.e.  
in your query the "validated" attribute came from the "Variations"  
section and the rest of the attributes came from the "Features"  
section).  The way around this is to perform two separate queries; one  
to select the features attributes and one to retrieve the variations  
attribute. You may also be able to link to two separate datasets, one  
for the validated part of the query and the other for the features  
part of the query and pull out all the information you need. I'm not  
sure how this is done using biomaRt, but perhaps someone else from the  
mailing list can help you to do this.
I hope that helps,
Regards,
Rhoda


